<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Vanilla Psycasts Expanded meditation focus on other mods' buildings: archotech structures and vanometric power
		sources give psyfocus strength, and royal furniture from vanilla, VFE Furniture and VFE Empire becomes a Wealth
		focus source that grows stronger with more royal furniture nearby.
		This folder only loads when VPE is active (see loadFolders.xml). Each partner mod's part is gated on its packageId;
		each part sits in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.

		Changes from the original, which gated each part with a PatchOperationFindMod on the mod's display name:
		- The VFE Empire op targeted `efName="VFEE_RoyalStool"`, a typo, so the royal stool never got its focus comp even
		  though it had the focus stat and was listed in every offset table. Corrected to defName.
		- The Alpha Biomes derelict structures already have a <statBases> node, so adding a second one logged a
		  duplicate-node error and the later node replaced their stats. The op now adds into the existing <statBases>.
		All 27 target defs were checked against the current VPE, VFE Furniture, VFE Empire, VFE Power, VFE Art, VGE,
		Alpha Biomes and vanilla 1.6 defs; no installed mod already makes any of them a meditation focus source.
		Split by category into the MMMM Integrations sub-mods: this copy holds the Traits ops plus VPE's pointsOnly flips, which the trait grants need, so the two stay together.
	-->
	<!--
		Focus types for traits: VPE's Group, Science and Wealth meditation focus types become available to pawns with
		matching traits (Kind, Greedy, Too Smart, and traits from VTE, VRE Highmate and The Sims Traits). VPE marks these
		three types pointsOnly, which makes its PawnCanUse postfix refuse them unless bought with psycast points, so the
		trait grants only work together with the pointsOnly flip; the two stay one block.
		In the original this sat behind a Too Many Mods setting (TMM_VPE_FocusTypeForTraits, default on). The setting is
		dropped: this mod is the opt-in now.
		Verified against VPE, VTE, VRE Highmate and vanilla 1.6: all three focus defs ship pointsOnly=true, and every trait
		target has one degree with no focus types yet. The Sims Traits is not installed, so its three operations are
		unverified.
	-->
	<!-- VPE: let the Group, Science and Wealth focus types be granted by traits, not only bought with points -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/MeditationFocusDef[defName="VPE_Group"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.MeditationFocusExtension"]/pointsOnly</xpath>
		<value>
			<pointsOnly>false</pointsOnly>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/MeditationFocusDef[defName="VPE_Science"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.MeditationFocusExtension"]/pointsOnly</xpath>
		<value>
			<pointsOnly>false</pointsOnly>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/MeditationFocusDef[defName="VPE_Wealth"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.MeditationFocusExtension"]/pointsOnly</xpath>
		<value>
			<pointsOnly>false</pointsOnly>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/TraitDef[defName="Kind"]/degreeDatas/li</xpath>
		<value>
			<allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
				<li>VPE_Group</li>
			</allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/TraitDef[defName="Greedy"]/degreeDatas/li</xpath>
		<value>
			<allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
				<li>VPE_Wealth</li>
			</allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/TraitDef[defName="TooSmart"]/degreeDatas/li</xpath>
		<value>
			<allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
				<li>VPE_Science</li>
			</allowedMeditationFocusTypes>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
